course: dictionary
lesson: 2505
title: A decade: ten years or a group of ten
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A decade is a period of ten years. When a text says «Ireland has sent peacekeepers for decades», the word decades tells you it has happened for a very long time, many periods of ten years.
explain: Decade has a second meaning too: a group of ten, like the ten beads on a rosary. To choose the right meaning, read the sentence and ask: is it talking about years, or about a set of ten things?
explain: Look for number clues. «Bamboo flowers and dies all at once every few decades» tells you it happens rarely, not every year. Check your meaning by swapping in "ten years": if it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: A decade is a period of ten years.
fact: Decades is the plural: two decades is 20 years, and "for decades" means for a very long time.
fact: A decade can also be a group of ten, like the ten beads on a rosary.
fact: «The eighties» means the decade from 1980 to 1989, not 80 years ago.
fact: «The noughties» means the decade from 2000 to 2009.
exercise: «Ireland has sent peacekeepers for decades.» What does decades mean here? | *Many periods of ten years, a very long time | A group of ten soldiers | Exactly ten days | Three weeks
exercise: «The eighties» means which years? | 80 years ago | 1880 to 1889 | *1980 to 1989 | 2080 to 2089
exercise: Besides a period of ten years, what else can a decade be? | A tiny bead | A group of a hundred | A week of school | *A group of ten, like ten beads on a rosary
test: «A girl's parrot could live for decades.» What does decades mean? | A short walk | Ten parrots | Ten days | *Long periods of ten years
test: A decade ago means about how long back? | *About ten years ago | Ten days ago | A hundred years ago | Just this morning
exam: «The next decade» means what? | *The next ten years | The last hundred years | Tomorrow | The next ten minutes
